      "content": "i see. so it's a lot of different factors clashing. since im doing a historiography paper, i want to make sure i'm not missing any big perspectives. some of the sources i've seen online go really hard on the idea that the establishment of the state was fundamentally a colonial project that ignored local rights, while others say it was a necessary act of national liberation for a persecuted people. from an academic standpoint, is there a consensus on which of those frameworks is more accurate, or are they both seen as equally valid ways to interpret the history?",
